seq v=1 rig=screen program=claude build=2.1.0
# E8: Esc on a box whose footer says `Esc to cancel` chooses its cancel, which
# rejects the call: the close is `declined` at conf=heuristic when the screen
# reports nothing more. When the screen reports the interrupt the box was
# stopped under (`esc-declines-the-box.seq`), that report is the program's own
# word after the key, and the close is `declined` at conf=strong.
see busy
half
see prompt bash:not-read-only fixture=claude-2.1.280-box-bash-touch
expect open p1 approval par=t1 box=bash:not-read-only @500
person key=esc chose=decline
at 700 see idle
expect close p1 approval out=declined by=human conf=heuristic @700
at 3000 see busy
see prompt bash:not-read-only fixture=claude-2.1.280-box-bash-touch
expect open p2 approval par=t2 box=bash:not-read-only
admit ctl key=esc chose=decline
accept
interrupted
see idle fixture=claude-2.1.316-box-bash-declined-esc
expect close p2 approval out=declined by=ctl conf=strong
